%% TEST-NAME: test-equations-shared-align
%% TEST-WHAT: Pin the KNOWN-BROKEN behaviour of equations=shared mode
%%            inside align/gather: the atom counter advances once per
%%            equation line, which is rarely what the author wants.
%% TEST-SOURCE: REVIEW_E #6 (MAJOR), REVIEW_F R2, DESIGN.md open issues
%% TEST-SECTION: DESIGN.md §Equation numbering, §Package options
%% TEST-EXIT: 0
%% TEST-PINS-KNOWN-BROKEN: yes
%% TEST-LOG-NOT: semtex.*Error|Undefined control sequence
%% TEST-SBL-CONTAINS: \semtex@sbl@end{OK}
%% TEST-PACKAGES: amsmath,amsthm,semtex
%% TEST-RERUN: 2
%%
%% REVIEW_E finding #6 (MAJOR) identifies equations=shared as a
%% hazard in align/gather/split/\subequations. In shared mode
%% the equation counter is \let-aliased to the atom counter,
%% so every \\ line in an align that triggers an equation
%% number also steps the atom counter. The fixture documents
%% this known-broken behaviour so the runner can warn but not
%% fail. Recommended user default remains equations=separate.
%%
%% This test is INTENTIONALLY documenting a hazard, not
%% enforcing a "correct" count. TEST-PINS-KNOWN-BROKEN: yes
%% tells the runner to tolerate whatever the count turns out
%% to be so long as compilation exits 0 and the sbl end marker
%% fires.

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\usepackage{amsthm}
\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}[section]
\usepackage[equations=shared]{semtex}
\semtextrack{theorem}

\begin{document}
\START

\section{Equations shared hazard}

Lead paragraph. In shared mode this is atom 1.something; the
exact number depends on whether pdflatex has yet triggered
\refstepcounter via the para/begin hook.

\begin{align}
  a_1 &= b_1, \label{eq:line1} \\
  a_2 &= b_2, \label{eq:line2} \\
  a_3 &= b_3. \label{eq:line3}
\end{align}

Trailing paragraph. In shared mode, multiple atom counter
ticks will have fired between the lead and trailing paras
(one per align line). This behaviour is documented, not
tested for a specific count.

\END
\end{document}
